# Math Game Conventions

Every game lives at `games/<game-slug>.html`. Each game must link the two shared files **before** any local `<style>` or `<script>`:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../shared/mf-design.css">
<style>/* only this game's scene + custom widgets */</style>
...
<script src="../shared/mf-core.js"></script>
<script>/* STRINGS + generators + main(), all using MF.* helpers */</script>
```

No other external libraries, fonts, or build tools. The only allowed local assets are the reward images in `images/`.

## MF.* shared helper API

`window.MF` is exposed by `shared/mf-core.js`. Destructure what you need at the top of each game's script:

```js
const { rand, pick, shuffle, makeDistractors,
        turkishWord, renderBlocks,
        loadRewards, chooseReward, mountReward,
        spawnConfetti, trapFocus, releaseFocus,
        createI18n } = MF;
```

| Helper | Signature | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `rand(a, b)` | `(number, number) → number` | Random integer in [a, b] |
| `pick(arr)` | `(T[]) → T` | Random element |
| `shuffle(arr)` | `(T[]) → T[]` | Shuffled copy |
| `makeDistractors(answer, count, opts?)` | `opts: {min?, max?}` | Pedagogical distractors for MC questions |
| `turkishWord(n)` | `(0..100) → string` | Turkish number word |
| `renderBlocks(n)` | `(number) → string` | HTML for base-10 block display |
| `loadRewards(defaults?, url?)` | `async` | Fetch `../config.json`; returns `{ list }` store |
| `chooseReward(list)` | `(list) → reward` | Weighted random selection |
| `mountReward(wrapEl, reward, missingLabel)` | — | Preload image, attach or show fallback |
| `spawnConfetti(layerEl, colors?)` | — | Fill confetti layer with 60 pieces |
| `trapFocus(modal)` / `releaseFocus(modal)` | — | Keyboard focus trap for reward modal |
| `createI18n(strings, storageKey?)` | — | I18n factory (optional; most games keep their own `STRINGS`) |

**Standard reward loading pattern** (replaces the old manual `REWARDS` array + `fetch`):

```js
const rewardStore = MF.loadRewards();   // kicks off config.json fetch; list auto-updates
// ...
const reward = MF.chooseReward(rewardStore.list);
MF.mountReward($rewardImageWrap, reward, S('rewardMissing'));
MF.spawnConfetti($confettiLayer);
```

## Bilingual (EN + TR) is mandatory

Every game **must** ship with both English and Turkish strings and a header language toggle. Pattern (copy from `@games/number_city.html`):

```js
const STRINGS = {
  en: { title: '...', instruction1: '...', praises: ['Great!','Awesome!'], wrongMsg: (a)=>`Answer was ${a}`, rewardTitle: 'You Won!', playAgain: 'Play Again', langToggle: 'TR', /* ... */ },
  tr: { title: '...', instruction1: '...', praises: ['Harika!','Süper!'],  wrongMsg: (a)=>`Cevap ${a} idi`,    rewardTitle: 'Kazandın!', playAgain: 'Tekrar Oyna', langToggle: 'EN', /* ... */ },
};
let lang = localStorage.getItem('mf_lang') || 'tr';   // tr is the default
const S = (k, ...a) => { const v = STRINGS[lang][k]; return typeof v === 'function' ? v(...a) : v; };
```

- Default language is **Turkish**. Persist in `localStorage` under a key prefixed `mf_` (e.g. `mf_lang`).
- Language toggle button lives in the header and shows the *other* language code.
- Re-render the current question after switching language so visible text updates immediately.
- Every game has a meaningful bilingual title (e.g. EN: "Number City", TR: "Sayı Şehri").

## Game loop

- **Infinite randomized loop** — no fixed question count, no end-of-round score. The game ends only when the progress bar fills.
- Configurable constants at the top of the script:

```js
const TARGET_PROGRESS = 10;
const INCREMENT_RIGHT = 1;
const DECREMENT_WRONG = 0;   // never below 0; pick 0 or 1 based on age
const FEEDBACK_DELAY  = 1100;
```

- Correct answer: increment progress, show praise, animate `correctPulse`, advance.
- Wrong answer: decrement (clamped to 0), show supportive message that includes the correct answer, animate `wrongShake`, advance.
- Progress bar uses the red→yellow→green gradient (see `@.cursor/rules/design-spirit.mdc`).

## Reward modal

When `progress >= TARGET_PROGRESS`:
1. Show modal with `popIn` animation, confetti layer, focus-trapped, ESC closes/restarts.
2. Use `MF.loadRewards()` + `MF.chooseReward()` + `MF.mountReward()` (see MF.* API above).
   - Default fallback list: `1tl.jpg (w:10)`, `5tl.jpg (w:50)`, `10tl.jpg (w:20)`, `20tl.jpg (w:20)`.
3. **Path is `../images/<file>.jpg`, NOT `images/<file>.jpg`.** Games live in `games/`, so a bare `images/...` resolves to `games/images/...` in the browser. `MF.loadRewards()` normalizes paths automatically.
4. **`MF.mountReward` preloads then attaches** the `<img>` — only appends to the DOM in `onload`, so a missing image shows the emoji fallback alone (no broken-image glyph).
5. On image error a friendly emoji fallback with the label and the localized "missing image" string is shown.
6. "Play Again" button (bilingual) resets progress to 0 and starts a new loop.

> **Reward filenames on disk:** `1tl.jpg`, `5tl.jpg`, `10tl.jpg`, `20tl.jpg` (and an unused `5tltl.jpg`). Always use `../images/5tl.jpg` (not `5tlt.jpg`, not `5tltl.jpg`).

## Accessibility & input

- ARIA labels on every interactive element, localized through `STRINGS`.
- Keyboard support: digits + Backspace + Enter for numpad questions, `A`/`B`/`C` for multiple choice.
- Touch targets ≥ 90px tall. `user-select: none`, `-webkit-tap-highlight-color: transparent` on `<body>`.
- `<meta viewport>` with `user-scalable=no`. Responsive via `clamp()` and a `max-width: 500px` breakpoint.

## File header

Start every game's local `<style>` block with a banner like:

```css
/* =============================================================
   <GAME NAME EN> / <GAME NAME TR> — Grade <N> Math Game
   Target concept: <plain-English concept summary>
   Curriculum: MAT.<x>.<y>.<z>
   ============================================================= */
```

## Lessons learned (from real bugs caught in review)

These are real mistakes that have shipped in this project. Read them before writing or editing a game.

### 1. Reward image paths are `../images/...`, never `images/...`

Games live in `games/<slug>.html`. A relative URL like `<img src="images/1tl.jpg">` resolves to `games/images/1tl.jpg` in the browser — that folder doesn't exist, so every reward silently falls back to "(reward image missing)". Always use `../images/<file>.jpg`.

> Symptom: reward modal always shows the 🪙 emoji fallback even though the files are on disk at the project root.

### 2. Preload the reward image; only append `<img>` on success

The naive pattern `img.src = ...; wrap.appendChild(img);` causes the broken-image glyph to flash next to the fallback when the load fails. Set `img.onload` to be the moment you append, and `img.onerror` to swap the wrap's `innerHTML` to the fallback markup. Do not append the `<img>` eagerly.

### 3. Every visible TR/EN string lives in `STRINGS`, even the ones that "look the same"

ARIA labels, count labels, summary words (`onluk` / `birlik`, `tens` / `ones`), zone titles, toast messages, regroup announcements — **all** of them must flow through `S('key')`. Anything you hard-code in HTML or in a `gen*` function will silently stay in one language when the user toggles. Audit by checking every Turkish phrase is unique to the STRINGS table only.

### 4. Turkish unit words are `onluk` / `birlik`, not `onlar` / `birler`

`onlar` / `birler` are plural pronouns ("them" / "ones-the"). The base-ten unit words are **`onluk`** (a "ten") and **`birlik`** (a "one") — both singular, both used as `3 onluk + 2 birlik = 32`. Header chips can pluralize visually (`ONLUKLAR`, `BİRLİKLER`) but the inline summary uses the singular form.

### 5. Don't put two `id` attributes on one element

Easy to do when you're piecing together a button: `<button id="checkBtn" id="checkLabel">`. Browsers silently take the first one; the second never resolves and any `getElementById('checkLabel')` returns `null`, crashing later. Lint catches it. So do you, if you re-read the diff.

### 6. Don't overload state field names mid-refactor

If `state.locked` is a boolean lock-flag used everywhere as `if (state.locked) return;`, do not later reassign it to an object like `{ tens: 0, ones: 0 }` for a different purpose. Add a new field (e.g. `state.prefill`, `state.readOnly`) instead. Overloading silently makes every old check truthy and breaks the game in subtle ways.

### 7. Localize ARIA labels too

Aria text like `aria-label="Add one ten"` is read aloud by screen readers; it must switch with the language toggle. Put every ARIA string in `STRINGS` and re-apply them in `applyStaticStrings()`.

### 8. After a regroup, clamp any prefilled counts

In modes where the workspace starts with pre-filled blocks (e.g. `buildPartial`), automatic 10-ones-to-1-ten regrouping can consume some of the pre-filled ones. The pre-fill counter must be clamped (`prefill.ones = Math.min(prefill.ones, workspace.ones)`) so the remove button doesn't stay incorrectly disabled or enabled.
